        {
          "id": "et_pb_row_12",
          "hiddenOn": [],
          "columns": [
            {
              "size": "1_2",
              "modules": [
                {
                  "type": "testimonial",
                  "id": "et_pb_testimonial_0",
                  "author": "Rebecca P",
                  "meta": "",
                  "html": "<p><span>Fab little find. Lovely cottage with everything you need for a weekend get away. Games room an added bonus and cottage kitted out for all your needs. Clean with linen provided, plenty of room for 6 of us and didn’t feel cramped.</span></p>",
                  "portrait": "/media/2020/09/Screenshot-2020-09-16-at-11.44.01.png",
                  "hiddenOn": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "testimonial",
                  "id": "et_pb_testimonial_1",
                  "author": "Pho3nix1705",
                  "meta": "",
                  "html": "<p><span>We spent a lovely weekend in Swallow cottage. Just perfect for a group of friends looking for some time in the country to relax and catch up. We arrived to a very warm welcome from Liz and were shown to our cottage which was comfy, clean and tidy. Cottages are located on a working farm and the games room was a great place to relax and play a few games! Highly recommend to anyone looking for a break away from busy life – fantastic location, charming cottages and friendly owners!</span></p>",
                  "portrait": "/media/2020/09/Screenshot-2020-09-16-at-11.53.50.png",
                  "hiddenOn": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "size": "1_2",
              "modules": [
                {
                  "type": "testimonial",
                  "id": "et_pb_testimonial_2",
                  "author": "Burl Brown",
                  "meta": "",
                  "html": "<div> <div> <p><span>We stayed here whilst visiting family in the area and couldn’t have asked for more. They are beautifully converted cottages, with everything you could need amongst stunning countryside. Great routes for walks or runs in the countryside, perfect for building up an appetite. Will definitely be back!</span></p> </div> </div>",
                  "portrait": "/media/2020/09/Screenshot-2020-09-16-at-11.47.14.png",
                  "hiddenOn": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "testimonial",
                  "id": "et_pb_testimonial_3",
                  "author": "Mrs G Dundee",
                  "meta": "",
                  "html": "<p><span>Stayed here for 2 nights as husband had a course nearby and we chose this for convenience. The property is dog friendly and lots of grounds to explore. Cottage is perfect for needs, basic but more than ample… Also very reasonable price. Great location for nearby towns and local pubs….would recommend The Sun Inn in Everton.. Excellent pub food and very reasonable. We will definitely return in the future and would like to stay longer.</span></p>",
                  "portrait": "/media/2020/09/Screenshot-2020-09-16-at-11.56.08.png",
                  "hiddenOn": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
